(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The GIL and the threads' state (PY6f; PYS10 (a); Python/ceval_gil.c, Python/pystate.c). One Python thread runs"] [10 1 "// at a time: the goroutine holding the GIL. current (frame.go) is its *Thread, swapped on taking the GIL as"] [11 1 "// CPython swaps _PyThreadState_Current, so the object model needs no locks and currentThread() is right in every"] [12 1 "// goroutine that holds it. The GIL is inactive until the first thread starts: the starter becomes its holder then,"] [13 1 "// so a program of one thread only pays the eval breaker's load. A waiter asks the holder to drop it after"] [14 1 "// sys.getswitchinterval() (gil_drop_request); the holder drops it at its next check of the eval breaker (a frame's"] [15 1 "// start, a backward jump: eval.go) and waits until another thread took it (FORCE_SWITCHING). Blocking Go that"] [16 1 "// touches no Python object runs with the GIL released (allowThreads, blockOn: Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS)."] [18 1 "// the eval breaker's bits (evalBreaker, eval.go)"] [20 29 "// another thread waits for the GIL"] [21 29 "// a signal is pending (handled on the main thread)"] [22 29 "// a thread has an asynchronous exception (PyThreadState_SetAsyncExc, queue 598)"] [23 29 "// finalize.go's queue holds dead objects (drained by the GIL's holder)"] [24 29 "// a sys.monitoring tool has events (queue 220: monitoring.go's frame starts; 16, as 218's finalizers took 8)"] [28 1 "// evalBreaker is CPython's eval_breaker, the bits above: the loop (eval.go) calls handleEvalBreaker when it is"] [29 1 "// non-zero at a frame's start (RESUME) and at a backward jump (JUMP_BACKWARD)."] [32 1 "// switchInterval is sys.getswitchinterval() in nanoseconds."] [37 1 "// getSwitchInterval and setSwitchInterval are sys.getswitchinterval and sys.setswitchinterval."] [50 13 "// CPython keeps microseconds"] [58 22 "// the GIL was dropped"] [59 22 "// a thread took it"] [60 22 "// a thread was started: the GIL is in use"] [63 18 "// takes so far"] [64 18 "// threads waiting in take"] [65 18 "// gil_drop_request"] [66 2 "// final is the thread finalizing the interpreter (queue 253): any other that takes the GIL hangs"] [67 2 "// (_PyThreadState_MustExit, PyThread_hang_thread)"] [71 1 "// finalize makes t the only thread that may run Python from now on (_PyRuntimeState_SetFinalizing)."] [87 1 "// activate makes the GIL used, held by t (the running thread, which starts the first other thread)."] [97 1 "// take waits for the GIL and makes t the running thread (take_gil)."] [102 3 "// the timed wait of take_gil: each interval in which the holder has not changed asks it to drop the GIL;"] [103 3 "// one that changed starts a new interval (the timer, re-armed by itself, under g.mu)"] [134 3 "// the interpreter is finalizing: this thread hangs, the GIL passed on (a forced drop waiting for a switch"] [135 3 "// is let go)"] [156 26 "// queue 230: the active interpreter's registers"] [160 1 "// release drops the GIL (drop_gil); with force, it waits until another thread took it when one waits."] [174 1 "// dropRequested is whether another thread asked for the GIL."] [181 1 "// allowThreads runs f, blocking Go that touches no Python object, with the GIL released."] [193 1 "// blockOn waits, with the GIL released, until a value can be received from ch (received: true), the timeout"] [194 1 "// passes (a negative one never does: false), or, on the main thread, a signal arrives: its handlers then run"] [195 1 "// with the GIL (an exception from one ends the wait) and the wait goes on for the time left. ch nil waits for"] [196 1 "// the timeout or a signal alone."] [247 1 "// sleepFor is time.sleep: d with the GIL released, interruptible by a signal's handler (PEP 475: the sleep goes"] [248 1 "// on after a handler that returns)."] [258 1 "// handleEvalBreaker is the eval breaker's work (eval.go: a frame's start and a backward jump, the breaker non-zero):"] [259 1 "// the GIL yielded on a drop request, the pending signals' handlers run on the main thread."] [285 4 "// the main thread handles signals: let it run"] [293 1 "// threadInfo is a thread's state beyond Thread's own fields (PyThreadState's): touched under the GIL only."] [298 23 "// the thread-local objects that hold a dict for it"] [299 2 "// asyncExc is the exception PyThreadState_SetAsyncExc set for the thread (queue 598): raised at its next check of the"] [300 2 "// eval breaker"] [307 2 "// threadsRunning is the number of threads started and not finished (_thread._count)"] [311 1 "// threadInfoOf is t's state, made on first use: the main thread's ident is mainThreadIdent."] [327 1 "// isMainThread is whether t is its interpreter's main thread (the one that handles signals)."] [332 1 "// ExtSetAsyncExc is PyThreadState_SetAsyncExc (Python/pystate.c, queue 598): the exception exc (a class or an instance; nil"] [333 1 "// clears it) raised in the thread whose ident is id at its next check of the eval breaker; the number of thread states"] [334 1 "// changed, 0 when no live thread has that ident."] [348 1 "// updateAsyncExcBit sets the eval breaker's asynchronous exception bit while a thread has one pending."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[236 34] [269 26] [313 25]]} (go/file "thread_gil.go" :imports [


